Test Architecture

Feature Files
      ↓
Step Definitions
      ↓
API Services / Page Objects
      ↓
Application / API

Feature Files

Feature files describe test scenarios using Gherkin.

Given an authenticated user exists

When I create a shopping cart

Then the cart should be created successfully

Step Definitions

Step definitions contain the implementation of Gherkin steps.

When(
  "I create a shopping cart with the product",
  function () {

    const cart = {
      produtos: [
        {
          idProduto: this.productId,
          quantidade: 1,
        },
      ],
    };

    return CartService.createCart(
      cart,
      this.token
    ).then((response) => {
      this.response = response;
    });

  }
);

API Services

API services centralize HTTP requests.

createCart(cart, token) {

  return cy.request({

    method: "POST",

    url: `${Cypress.expose("apiUrl")}/carrinhos`,

    headers: {
      Authorization: token,
    },

    body: cart,

    failOnStatusCode: false,

  });

}

This approach improves:

Code reuse

Test maintainability

Test readability

Separation of responsibilities

API request organization

